<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 56,778 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 56,778 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 56,778 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Thursday compared to 39,481 tonnes in the same period on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Thursday    June 4</p>
<p>    Export cargo		 9,146	 5,939</p>
<p>    Import cargo		47,632	33,542</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, four ships sailed and nine berthed. In the next 24 hours, four are expected to sail and seven are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	Tonnes/TEUs  Ship			Berthing</p>
<p>Crude oil	    66,000	 Johar			5/6</p>
<p>Gas oil		60,000	 New Tatina		 7/6</p>
<p>Palm oil		9,000	 Jian She-32		7/6</p>
<p>Vehicles		  100	 Hual Margarita	   Due</p>
<p>Palm oil	     10,000	 Wawasan Courage	 10/6</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
